# Celestial Reunion's additional cost needs two creatures of one type to behold (CR 601.2b-c): Bot1 holds an Elvish Mystic, a
# Birds of Paradise and a Nameless Inversion (a Kindred Instant with changeling, so every creature type, and an Elf), with the mana
# for X = 1 in the pool, and no two creatures share a type: the Nameless Inversion is no creature (a ruling), so the attempted cost cannot be paid and its cast is reversed. Reunion can then be cast without it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Celestial Reunion
Elvish Mystic
Birds of Paradise
Nameless Inversion
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Celestial Reunion.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Modes(Choose a creature type and behold two creatures of that type)
Bot1.Choose(Confirm X)
? Bot1.Hand = Celestial Reunion; Elvish Mystic; Birds of Paradise; Nameless Inversion; Forest
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot1.Mana = {B}{G}
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Jet
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = true
? Stack.Count = 0
? Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand.Celestial Reunion.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Modes(Cast without choosing a type)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Search(Elvish Mystic)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Elvish Mystic; Birds of Paradise; Nameless Inversion; Forest; Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Graveyard = Celestial Reunion
